had remained incomplete for decades. Applications in medicine or crop protection may still be further

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:58.300
down the road, but the foundation is now solid. From biological chemistry, we move to fundamental physics,

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:03.300
where a question that's lingered for four decades has finally received convincing experimental

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:09.140
confirmation. The Cardar Parisi Zhang equation, a theoretical model describing how surfaces grow

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:14.160
and roughen over time, has now been verified in real two-dimensional systems ranging from growing

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:19.460
crystals to bacterial colonies. For years, the KPZ equation was a beautiful piece of mathematics that

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:24.040
